{
  "study": "AuthBridge plugin overhead — designed experiment (supersedes the retrospective mining of the 12-run matrix)",
  "why": [
    "The 12-run matrix runs each preset ONCE at max_tasks=5. Bootstrapping the v1.26+v1.27 samples shows that",
    "buys no resolving power at all: no preset-to-preset difference below 3x is detectable, and the per-leg",
    "median of a judged/unjudged MIXTURE is a step function of the judged count rather than an estimate of",
    "anything. Worse, the 50-task baseline leg shows the first 5 tasks cost 2.1x (OCP) to 3.0x (KinD) more per",
    "task than steady state WITH NO SIDECAR AT ALL, so every n=5 'fixed cost per task' figure is warm-up.",
    "This file fixes the three defects that matter: n, replication, and run order.",
    "",
    "#111 is the decisive security test and runs FIRST because it is the cheapest and the only one with a",
    "security consequence: ibac-only at max_parallel_sessions=1. Serial execution means decision caching shows",
    "~1 judge call for the whole leg, while no caching shows one per tool call. Across four matrices, 12 IBAC",
    "legs, only one ever reached 5/5 judged, and the counts wobble randomly across identical configs -- the",
    "signature of a race, which is either benign caching or a FAIL-OPEN enforcement gap.",
    "",
    "#101-#110 are two replicates of the five gsm8k conditions at max_tasks=50. n=50 amortises the warm-up",
    "transient (visible and gone by task ~10), so per-task cost splits into a one-time admission cost and a",
    "steady-state marginal cost -- a decomposition n=5 cannot express. It also lifts the minimum detectable",
    "preset-to-preset difference from '3x, i.e. nothing' to roughly 10-30%.",
    "",
    "ORDER IS THE POINT of running the second replicate in reverse. In the 12-run the legs run in a fixed",
    "sequence, so gateway warm-up and response caching alias perfectly onto the plugin variable -- demonstrably",
    "so on the LLM path, which is why those spans are excluded from the headline. Reversing replicate 2 makes",
    "every condition's mean run position identical (11), so a monotone drift over the session cancels instead",
    "of loading onto one preset.",
    "",
    "#112/#113 test the projection. The retrospective report multiplies a gsm8k per-call delta by tool-call",
    "count to project tau2 at ~25.6s/task and appworld at ~37.3s/task, assuming per-call cost is constant",
    "across benchmarks. tau2 makes ~11 tool calls per task against gsm8k's 1, so this matched pair MEASURES",
    "that instead of assuming it. It is also the leg most likely to fail outright: the preset chain has only",
    "ever been exercised on gsm8k."
  ],
  "order": [111, 101, 102, 103, 104, 105, 106, 107, 108, 109, 110, 112, 113],
  "legs": [
    {
      "n": 111,
      "bench": "gsm8k",
      "role": "serial-diagnostic",
      "condition": "ibac-only",
      "rep": 0,
      "title": "111 — DIAGNOSTIC: gsm8k --plugin-preset ibac-only --max-tasks 10 --max-parallel-sessions 1 — caching vs fail-open",
      "reading": "10 serial tool calls. ~1-2 judge calls => decision caching (benign). ~10 => no caching, and the judged/tool gaps seen under p=4 are a FAIL-OPEN gap.",
      "deploy": "DELETE gsm8k; POST deploy {\"authbridge_enabled\":true,\"plugin_preset\":\"ibac-only\"}",
      "deploy_body": {
        "agent": "tool_calling",
        "namespace": "team1",
        "authbridge_enabled": true,
        "plugin_preset": "ibac-only"
      },
      "teardown": true,
